      "run": 4,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "Upon arriving in the cramped galley with salt everywhere, I decided to take the kettle found on the floor. Proceeding north into a storage area that smelled strongly of paraffin, I examined a stiff coil of rope which was likely ruined by salt. I elected to take the rope with me and then ventured east to a landing. Here, I discovered a brass key lying on the floor and decided to pocket it.\n\nContinuing upwards, I reached a lamp room encased in glass, with stairs leading down and a gantry running west. In this room, I observed a logbook, presumably for keeping records, which I took upon examining its ruled columns, most of which were empty. \n\nAfter deliberating over the items collected, I returned south to the landing, then west back to the store. The shelves were largely vacant, confirming the sparse stock. At this point, I considered the possibility of using the brass key for some purpose but did not find an immediate opportunity to do so. The journey through the vessel concluded with a sense of having gathered useful items \u2014 the kettle, the rope",
